<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reciprocal Guarantee of Two Nations</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1791">1791</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Reciprocal Guarantee of Two Nations was an act adopted by the Great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejm">Sejm</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> on 20 October 1791, as an amendment to the Constitution of 3 May. It confirmed the union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> as a federation of equal partners and guaranteed Lithuania equal representation in the joint government and treasury. It was overturned with the constitution after 1792.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reciprocal-guarantee-of-two-nations.jpg" alt="Reciprocal Guarantee of Two Nations" width="320" height="491" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stanisław August Poniatowski · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zar%C4%99czenie_wzajemne_20_october_1791_Warsaw.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
